  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DeepSeek Harness GenUI",
      "text": "[](https://dsh-insights.com/p/pengyue-polaron/deepseek-harness-genui/)\n\nEnglish | [简体中文](README.zh-CN.md)\n\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-plugin-genui)\n[](package.json)\n[](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.29387)\n[](https://www.dsh.so/artifact/deepseek-harness-genui/)\n[](LICENSE)\n\n<img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pengyue-polaron/deepseek-harness-genui/main/assets/hero-en.png\" width=\"1280\" alt=\"DeepSeek Harness with an interactive day plan inline and a scientific model open in Canvas\">"
    },
    {
      "section": "DeepSeek Harness GenUI",
      "text": "DeepSeek Harness GenUI lets an Agent build a focused interface when a task is awkward in text. The Coding Agent writes ordinary React + TypeScript—not a component-tree DSL—and the interface can save user selections for the next Agent turn.\n\nThe result is a task-specific app that can explain a difficult relationship, collect connected choices, or continue a tool-backed workflow without asking the user to repeat their input."
    },
    {
      "section": "DeepSeek Harness GenUI",
      "text": "Related research: [*EvoGenUI-Bench: Evaluating LLMs as Multi-Turn Generative UI Assistants*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.29387)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Requires Node.js `^22.19.0 || ^24.0.0` and a supported DeepSeek Harness Web profile.\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-plugin-genui\ndsh --profile web\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "v0.15.2 supports Harness `0.2.1-rc.2` (npm `latest` checked on 2026-10-23) and `0.2.1-rc.3` (`next`), alongside the previously tested hosts. See the [compatibility report](docs/compatibility-2026-10-23.md) for validation and source-install instructions. Inline, Canvas, fullscreen, and localhost are supported. TUI/headless profiles are not supported. The local compiler uses WebAssembly and needs no install-script approval. Plugin users do not need Chrome or Chromium."
    },
    {
      "section": "Where It Helps",
      "text": "Use an interface when the user needs to see a complex relationship or make several connected choices. Plain questions, rewriting, summaries, and simple lists should stay in prose."
    },
    {
      "section": "Where It Helps",
      "text": "<table>\n  <tr>\n    <td><strong>Pick calendar slots</strong><br><br>Select useful writing blocks and save them to the task. A later calendar action remains separate and permission-gated.</td>\n    <td><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pengyue-polaron/deepseek-harness-genui/main/screenshots/en/calendar-planner.jpg\" width=\"280\" alt=\"English interface for choosing three writing slots\"></td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td><strong>Explore photosynthesis</strong><br><br>Move four causal controls and see the limiting step change immediately.</td>\n    <td><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pengyue-polaron/deepseek-harness-genui/main/screenshots/en/photosynthesis-explorer.jpg\" width=\"280\" alt=\"English interactive photosynthesis model with four causal controls\"></td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td><strong>Trace a code path</strong><br><br>Turn a source-grounded CLI explanation into a local explorer of files, functions, and branches.</td>\n    <td><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pengyue-polaron/deepseek-harness-genui/main/screenshots/en/code-path-explorer.jpg\" width=\"280\" alt=\"English source-grounded code path explorer returned from a CLI request\"></td>\n  </tr>\n</table>"
    },
    {
      "section": "The Core Loop",
      "text": "1. The Agent writes and builds a React + TypeScript app for the current task.\n2. The user saves meaningful values such as selections, form answers, drafts, or progress.\n3. A later Agent turn reads those values and continues the task.\n4. Connected tools and public HTTPS routes must be declared. Harness asks for task-scoped access, and undeclared calls are blocked."
    },
    {
      "section": "The Core Loop",
      "text": "Later edits update the same app. A candidate that fails the build or source checks does not replace the last working version; a crashing version is quarantined and rolled back when possible."
    },
    {
      "section": "Inline & Canvas",
      "text": "| Inline | Canvas |\n| --- | --- |\n| <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pengyue-polaron/deepseek-harness-genui/main/screenshots/en/code-path-inline.jpg\" width=\"620\" alt=\"An interactive code path shown inline in a DeepSeek Harness conversation\"> | <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pengyue-polaron/deepseek-harness-genui/main/screenshots/en/code-path-canvas.jpg\" width=\"620\" alt=\"The DeepSeek Harness sidebar, conversation, and code-path explorer visible together in the right-side Canvas\"> |\n| A compact control or focused choice. | More room without covering the conversation. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Inline & Canvas",
      "text": "Inline, Canvas, fullscreen, and localhost are different surfaces over the same task state."
    },
    {
      "section": "Try It",
      "text": "Start a new Web session and paste a prompt:\n\n```text\nPlan a Saturday route with a museum, a riverside garden, and dinner. Build an\ninterface where I can change the times and make the garden optional.\n```\n\n```text\nBuild an interactive double-slit experiment. Let me change wavelength, slit\nspacing, and screen distance and see the interference pattern update.\n```\n\nAfter saving something in the interface, ask:\n\n```text\nWhat did I just choose in the interface? Continue from the saved result.\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Try It",
      "text": "The useful proof is not only that an interface appears—it is that the next Agent turn can continue from the interaction."
    },
    {
      "section": "Why Code-First",
      "text": "Component-schema renderers are usually better for predictable cards, tables, charts, and forms. This plugin is for structures that cannot be known in advance: simulations, spatial tools, source explorers, and multi-step task apps whose saved result must continue the same Harness task."
    },
    {
      "section": "Why Code-First",
      "text": "The trade-off is deliberate: generated code is more expressive than a fixed component catalog, while this project remains DeepSeek Harness-specific rather than a cross-client UI protocol. See [`dsh-genui`](https://github.com/omdsh-dev/dsh-genui), [`dsh-visualize`](https://github.com/Nagi-ovo/dsh-visualize), [A2UI](https://a2ui.org/introduction/what-is-a2ui/), and [MCP Apps](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/apps/overview) for related approaches."
    },
    {
      "section": "DESIGN.md",
      "text": "Open **Settings → Built-in plugins → Generated app design** on current hosts (or **Settings → Plugins → Plugin configuration** on older hosts) to choose automatic design selection, use `material-3`, `apple-human-interface`, or `shadcn-ui`, or import a custom `DESIGN.md`. The file controls visual language, not page structure; React remains free to implement the interaction the task needs."
    },
    {
      "section": "Safety",
      "text": "Generated code runs in an opaque-origin sandbox. A trusted parent keeps the real task capability token and brokers only saved state, declared tools, and declared credential-free public HTTPS routes. MCP credentials never enter generated code. Temporary links and grants expire after 7 days, as does task state 7 days after its last update."
    },
    {
      "section": "Safety",
      "text": "This boundary protects host credentials and capabilities, but it cannot make malicious code safe to trust with data already authorized for it to read. Do not put secrets in generated-app state or grant access to data the app should not display. See [Security](SECURITY.md) for the threat model."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "Building from source requires pnpm 11:\n\n```sh\npnpm install\npnpm run typecheck\npnpm run build\npnpm test\n\n[Acceptance scenarios](examples/real-user-scenarios.md) · [Release notes](docs/release-notes-v0.15.2.md) · [Contributing](CONTRIBUTING.md) · MIT"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "Listed on [dsh-market](https://dshmarket.com/p/pengyue-polaron/deepseek-harness-genui/) · [dsh.so](https://www.dsh.so/artifact/deepseek-harness-genui/) · [awesome-dsh-plugin](https://awesome-dsh-plugin.com/p/pengyue-polaron/deepseek-harness-genui/) · [dsh.plus](https://www.dsh.plus/en/plugins/deepseek-harness-genui/)"
    },
    {
      "section": "DeepSeek Harness GenUI",
      "text": "[English](README.md) | 简体中文\n\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-plugin-genui)\n[](package.json)\n[](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.29387)\n[](https://www.dsh.so/zh/artifact/deepseek-harness-genui/)\n[](LICENSE)\n\n<img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pengyue-polaron/deepseek-harness-genui/main/assets/hero-zh-CN.png\" width=\"1280\" alt=\"DeepSeek Harness 同时展示保存过选择的路线 Inline 和银河尺度 Canvas\">"
    },
    {
      "section": "DeepSeek Harness GenUI",
      "text": "DeepSeek Harness GenUI 让 Agent 在文字不够好用时，为当前任务生成一个聚焦界面。Coding Agent 编写普通的 React + TypeScript，而不是组件树 DSL；界面可以把用户选择保存给下一轮 Agent。\n\n它适合讲清复杂关系、收集相互关联的选择，或在工具工作流中继续处理，而不必让用户重复输入。\n\n相关研究：[《EvoGenUI-Bench: Evaluating LLMs as Multi-Turn Generative UI Assistants》](https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.29387)。"
    },
    {
      "section": "安装",
      "text": "需要 Node.js `^22.19.0 || ^24.0.0` 和受支持的 DeepSeek Harness Web profile。\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-plugin-genui\ndsh --profile web\n```\n\nv0.15.2 支持 Harness `0.2.1-rc.2`（2026-10-23 核实的 npm `latest`）和 `0.2.1-rc.3`（`next`），同时保留此前验证过的宿主版本。验证范围及源码安装方法见[兼容性报告](docs/compatibility-2026-10-23.md)。支持 Inline、Canvas、全屏和 localhost；不支持 TUI/headless。本地编译器使用 WebAssembly，无需批准安装脚本；插件用户不需要安装 Chrome 或 Chromium。"
    },
    {
      "section": "适用场景",
      "text": "<table>\n  <tr>\n    <td><strong>选择日历时段</strong><br><br>选择写作时段并保存回任务。后续写入日历仍是独立且需要授权的操作。</td>\n    <td><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pengyue-polaron/deepseek-harness-genui/main/screenshots/zh-CN/calendar-planner.jpg\" width=\"280\" alt=\"选择三个写作时段的中文界面\"></td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td><strong>探索光合作用</strong><br><br>调整四个因果变量，直接观察限制环节如何变化。</td>\n    <td><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pengyue-polaron/deepseek-harness-genui/main/screenshots/zh-CN/photosynthesis-explorer.jpg\" width=\"280\" alt=\"可以改变四个条件的光合作用瓶颈模型\"></td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td><strong>追踪代码路径</strong><br><br>把基于真实源码的 CLI 解释变成文件、函数和分支都可探索的本地页面。</td>\n    <td><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/pengyue-polaron/deepseek-harness-genui/main/screenshots/zh-CN/code-path-explorer.jpg\" width=\"280\" alt=\"通过 CLI 请求生成的中文代码路径解释器\"></td>\n  </tr>\n</table>"
    },
    {
      "section": "核心闭环",
      "text": "1. Agent 为当前任务编写并构建 React + TypeScript 页面。\n2. 用户保存选择、表单答案、草稿或进度等有意义的结果。\n3. 下一轮 Agent 读取这些值并继续任务。\n4. 页面必须声明要使用的工具和公开 HTTPS 接口。Harness 负责按任务授权，未声明调用会被拒绝。\n\n后续修改会更新同一个页面。构建或源码检查失败的候选不会替换最后一个可用版本；启动崩溃的版本会被隔离，并在可能时回滚。"
    },
